<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karytaina</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Karytaina is a village in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a> in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, dominated by a castle on a crag above the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alpheios">Alpheios</a> river. It was the seat of a barony of the Principality of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaea">Achaea</a>, and its castle was built around 1254 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geoffrey-of-bruyeres">Geoffrey of Bruyères</a>, hero of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chronicle-of-the-morea">Chronicle of the Morea</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> took it in 1320, and in the Greek War of Independence it served as a stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodoros-kolokotronis">Theodoros Kolokotronis</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karytaina.jpg" alt="Karytaina" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nochoje · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Karytainaview.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
